      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It seems like the characters you've described are fairly standard for high-stakes political thrillers. I would categorize them as follows:\n\n- The character lineup feels most at home in a high-stakes political thriller, specifically ones focused on corrupt corporate and government elements.\n- The character with possibly the most potential to deviate from archetypes is Kenji, whose quiet and observant nature could suggest a different kind of backstory or skillset. This could add some nuance to our typical thriller characters.\n- The others, such as Claire and Andre, fit fairly neatly into stereotypes associated with high-stakes politics and exploitation.",
