      "content": "When I said Andre fits a stereotype of \"exploitation,\" I was referring to the common trope of the charismatic, intimidating figure in African-American communities who serves as a proxy for law enforcement or authority. This character is often used to bolster the voices and perspectives of other Black characters in vanilla narratives.\n\nAs for Kenji, I suggested he has potential to deviate from archetypes due to both his personality traits and his background. While his name and cultural background are traditionally East Asian, some of his character traits could fit neat categories (e.g., calm, observant, technical expertise). However, only you, as the writer, have agency to choose whether to categorize him based on his cultural background or to transcend those expectations, giving him a unique character beyond those roles.",
