      "content": "If you want to make this a gritty, realistic crime drama, Andre's character would be the most natural fit for a lead or primary antagonist role. His community background, \"difficult situation handling\" skills, and age would align with the conventional \"tough street guy\" trope often found in crime dramas. This type of narrative typically relies on relatable, gritty portrayals of hard-scrabble communities.\n\nAlternatively, you could consider Marcus as a lead or anti-hero, as his street-smart nature and community ties would complement the gritty crime drama genre. However, be cautious of reproducing African-American tropes without nuance and thoughtful character development.\n\nIt's essential to remember that casting these characters for the sake of expectation can feel formulaic and less true to their potential as well-rounded, complex individuals.",
